IMPORT prelude

-- Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (Cth) -- who is a dependant, a spouse, a child and a legal personal representative
-- (s 10, s 10A); the binding death benefit nomination the governing rules may permit, and the trustee-consent rule it is an exception
-- to (s 59); the purposes for which a regulated fund may be maintained, which fix whom a death benefit may go to and on what occasions
-- a member's benefit may be provided (s 62); where an undirected contribution goes (s 29WA); the 28-day remittance of amounts deducted
-- from pay (s 64); and insurance inside super: no default cover for inactive accounts, low balances or members under 25 unless they
-- elect it, and default death and permanent incapacity cover for MySuper members (ss 68AA, 68AAA-68AAF).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 131, compilation date 10 August 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 49, 2026 (register id C2026C00361,
-- in 2 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04633.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0007 in ../../../requirements.jsonl (priority 1): raised 8 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave scenarios (chloe c041, c04a, c082, c090; jake k094; daniel d074, d085, d093), which ask: where does the first
-- payslip's super go (citing "Part 7 (choice of fund; stapled fund)"); what insurance may a fund offer a 23-year-old, and what is the
-- default (s 68AAA); does a binding death benefit nomination lapse, and to whom may it direct the benefit (s 59(1A), reg 6.17A); what
-- lets a 60-year-old who keeps working, or a 60-year-old with a permanent incapacity, draw on super (the conditions of release); and
-- does the super go to a surviving spouse by nomination (s 59). SCOPED to those questions and the definitions, conditions and
-- exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- Most of what the lives ask is not in this Act. Part 7 of the SIS Act is "Provisions applying only to regulated superannuation
-- funds"; choice of fund and the stapled fund are in Part 3A of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992, and the life
-- cites that Act's ss 16 and 19 for the 11% rate (a separate subject). The conditions of release, preservation age, the definition of permanent incapacity,
-- the form of a nomination notice and its three-year lapse are all in the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations 1994,
-- which this Act empowers (ss 31(2)(g), (h), 59(1A), 10 "permanent incapacity") but which are NOT deposited. Every such matter is an
-- INPUT here: the age specified in the regulations, whether a member is taken to be permanently incapacitated, whether a nomination
-- notice complies with and remains in force under the regulations.
--
-- Not encoded: RSE licensing, MySuper authorisation, covenants (s 52), investment rules, the successor-fund transfer of elections (ss
-- 68AAA(2A), 68AAB(3A)-(3C), 68AAC(3A)-(3C)), the conditions of the employer-sponsor and dangerous occupation exceptions (ss 68AAE,
-- 68AAF, taken as INPUTS), the investment-direction exceptions in s 29WA(6), penalties (penalty units are not valued in this Act),
-- and everything in Parts 8 to 32.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive encodings (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public
-- use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 -- members, nominations and insurance`

§§ `10, 10A -- dependant, spouse, child, legal personal representative`

-- s 10: "dependant, in relation to a person, includes the spouse of the person, any child of the person and any person with whom the
-- person has an interdependency relationship." "spouse of a person includes: (a)" a person in a relationship registered under a
-- prescribed State or Territory law; "(b) another person who, although not legally married to the person, lives with the person on a
-- genuine domestic basis in a relationship as a couple." "child, in relation to a person, includes: (a) an adopted child, a stepchild
-- or an ex-nuptial child of the person; and (b) a child of the person's spouse; and (c)" a child within the Family Law Act 1975.
-- s 10A(1): an interdependency relationship if "(a) they have a close personal relationship; and (b) they live together; and (c) one or
-- each of them provides the other with financial support; and (d) one or each of them provides the other with domestic support and
-- personal care"; (2): or (a) alone, where they fail the others because of "a physical, intellectual or psychiatric disability".
--
-- All three definitions say "includes". A legally married spouse is a spouse in the ordinary sense, and the encoding treats one as such
-- (an inference: the Act's list does not mention marriage except to say the de facto partner is "not legally married"). A person who is
-- a dependant only in the ordinary (financial) sense is an INPUT flag; the Act does not define that sense.
DECLARE Relation HAS
    `is legally married to the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a registered relationship with the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with the member on a genuine domestic basis as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a child, adopted child, stepchild or ex-nuptial child of the member or of the member's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a close personal relationship with the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one gives the other financial support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one gives the other domestic support and personal care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fails the other requirements only because of a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a dependant in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the member's spouse` IF
        `the relation`'s `is legally married to the member`
    OR  `the relation`'s `is in a registered relationship with the member`
    OR  `the relation`'s `lives with the member on a genuine domestic basis as a couple`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has an interdependency relationship with the member` IF
        `the relation`'s `has a close personal relationship with the member`
    AND (    (    `the relation`'s `lives with the member`
              AND `the relation`'s `one gives the other financial support`
              AND `the relation`'s `one gives the other domestic support and personal care`)
         OR  `the relation`'s `fails the other requirements only because of a disability`)

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the member's dependant` IF
        `is the member's spouse` `the relation`
    OR  `the relation`'s `is a child, adopted child, stepchild or ex-nuptial child of the member or of the member's spouse`
    OR  `has an interdependency relationship with the member` `the relation`
    OR  `the relation`'s `is a dependant in the ordinary sense`

-- s 10: "legal personal representative means the executor of the will or administrator of the estate of a deceased person, the trustee
-- of the estate of a person under a legal disability or a person who holds an enduring power of attorney granted by a person."
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `executor of the member's will`
    `administrator of the member's estate`
    `trustee of the estate of a person under a legal disability`
    `holder of an enduring power of attorney granted by the member`
    `holder of an ordinary power of attorney`
    `no office`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a legal personal representative` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `holder of an ordinary power of attorney` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no office` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `59 -- discretions held by others; the binding death benefit nomination`

-- s 59(1): "Subject to subsection (1A), the governing rules of a superannuation entity other than a self managed superannuation fund
-- must not permit a discretion ... exercisable by a person other than a trustee ... to be exercised unless: (a) those rules require the
-- consent of the trustee" or (b) in an employer-sponsored fund, it relates to the employer-sponsor's contributions, solely to
-- terminating the fund, or circumstances covered by regulations. (2): inconsistent rules are "to the extent of the inconsistency,
-- invalid".
GIVEN `is a self managed superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the rules require the trustee's consent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an employer-sponsored fund` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `relates to employer-sponsor contributions, termination, or circumstances covered by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rule letting a non-trustee exercise the discretion is valid` IF
        `is a self managed superannuation fund`
    OR  `the rules require the trustee's consent`
    OR  (    `is an employer-sponsored fund`
         AND `relates to employer-sponsor contributions, termination, or circumstances covered by regulations`)

-- s 59(1A): "Despite subsection (1), the governing rules of a superannuation entity MAY, subject to a trustee of the entity complying
-- with any conditions contained in the regulations, permit a member of the entity, by notice given to a trustee of the entity in
-- accordance with the regulations, to require a trustee of the entity to provide any benefits in respect of the member on or after the
-- member's death to a person or persons mentioned in the notice, being the legal personal representative or a dependant or dependants
-- of the member."
--
-- The Act permits; it does not confer. The member can bind the trustee only if the fund's governing rules take up the permission, and
-- only by a notice that the regulations shape. Whether a notice "lapses" after three years (reg 6.17A, which the life cites) is not in
-- the Act: it arrives here as the INPUT `the notice complies with and remains in force under the regulations`.
GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation, `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be named in a binding nomination` IF
        `is the member's dependant` `the relation`
    OR  `is a legal personal representative` `the office`

GIVEN `the governing rules permit binding nominations` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the notice complies with and remains in force under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the trustee's conditions under the regulations are met` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the relation` IS A Relation,
      `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee is bound to pay the death benefit to the nominee` IF
        `the governing rules permit binding nominations`
    AND `the notice complies with and remains in force under the regulations`
    AND `the trustee's conditions under the regulations are met`
    AND `may be named in a binding nomination` `the relation` `the office`

§§ `62 -- the sole purpose test`

-- s 62(1)(a), the core purposes: benefits for each member "(i) on or after the member's retirement"; "(ii) on or after the member's
-- attainment of an age not less than the age specified in the regulations"; (iii) on the earlier of the two; "(iv)" and "(v)" benefits
-- on or after the member's death, if it occurred before retirement or before that age, and "the benefits are provided to the member's
-- legal personal representative, to any or all of the member's dependants, or to both".
-- s 62(1)(b), the ancillary purposes (only alongside a core purpose): "(i)" on termination of employment with an employer who had
-- contributed; "(ii) on or after the member's cessation of work ... on account of ill-health (whether physical or mental)"; (iii), (iv)
-- death after retirement or after that age, again to the legal personal representative or dependants; "(v) such other benefits as the
-- Regulator approves in writing".
--
-- The age "specified in the regulations" is an INPUT. So is whether a cessation of work was on account of ill-health. The Act's purpose
-- test says on which occasions a fund may provide benefits; when a particular member's benefit may actually be paid out is the payment
-- standard under s 31(2)(h), in the regulations (not deposited).
DECLARE Occasion IS ONE OF
    `retirement`
    `attaining the age specified in the regulations`
    `death`
    `termination of employment with a contributing employer`
    `cessation of work on account of ill-health`
    `a benefit the Regulator has approved in writing`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN Occasion,
      `the member has retired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the member's age` IS A NUMBER,
      `the age specified in the regulations` IS A NUMBER,
      `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serves a core purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `retirement` THEN `the member has retired`
    WHEN `attaining the age specified in the regulations` THEN `the member's age` AT LEAST `the age specified in the regulations`
    WHEN `death` THEN
            `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants`
        AND (    (NOT `the member has retired`)
             OR  `the member's age` LESS THAN `the age specified in the regulations`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN Occasion,
      `the member has retired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the member's age` IS A NUMBER,
      `the age specified in the regulations` IS A NUMBER,
      `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `serves an ancillary purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `termination of employment with a contributing employer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cessation of work on account of ill-health` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a benefit the Regulator has approved in writing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `death` THEN
            `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants`
        AND (    `the member has retired`
             OR  `the member's age` AT LEAST `the age specified in the regulations`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the occasion` IS AN Occasion,
      `the member has retired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the member's age` IS A NUMBER,
      `the age specified in the regulations` IS A NUMBER,
      `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund may be maintained to provide it` IF
        `serves a core purpose` `the occasion` `the member has retired` `the member's age` `the age specified in the regulations` `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants`
    OR  `serves an ancillary purpose` `the occasion` `the member has retired` `the member's age` `the age specified in the regulations` `paid to the legal personal representative or dependants`

§§ `29WA, 64 -- where a contribution goes, and when a deduction must reach the fund`

-- s 29WA(1)-(2): for a member "other than a defined benefit member", a contribution "in relation to which no direction has been given"
-- must be treated "as a contribution to be paid into a MySuper product of the fund". (4): a direction alleged to have been given after
-- 31 March 2013 "is taken not to have been given if: (a) the direction was not given in writing; or (b) a copy of the direction is not
-- held by or on behalf of the trustee".
GIVEN `is a defined benefit member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gave an investment direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the direction was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the trustee holds a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution goes into the MySuper product` IF
        (NOT `is a defined benefit member`)
    AND (    (NOT `gave an investment direction`)
         OR  (NOT `the direction was in writing`)
         OR  (NOT `the trustee holds a copy`))

-- s 64(1)-(2): where an employer is authorised to "deduct an amount from qualifying earnings, or from salary or wages" and pay it to a
-- regulated fund, "the employer must pay to a trustee of the superannuation fund the amount of the deduction before the end of the
-- 28-day period beginning immediately after the end of the month in which the deduction was made." (3), (3A): offences (100 and 50
-- penalty units). The section is about deductions from pay; the employer's own superannuation guarantee contribution is governed by
-- the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992, not here.
GIVEN `days after the end of the month of deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction was remitted in time` IF
    `days after the end of the month of deduction` AT MOST 28

§§ `68AA, 68AAA-68AAF -- insurance inside super`

-- s 68AAA(1): no benefit by "taking out or maintaining insurance" under a choice or MySuper product if "(a) the member's account is
-- inactive ... for a continuous period of 16 months" and the member has not elected cover under (2). (3): inactive = the trustee has
-- "not received an amount in respect of the member" in the period. (6): not for (a) a defined benefit member, (b), (c) permanent or
-- continuous full-time ADF Super members, "(d) a member to whom the employer-sponsor contribution exception applies".
-- s 68AAB(1): the same bar if "(a) the member has an account balance ... less than $6,000; and (b) on or after 1 November 2019, the
-- member has not had an account balance ... equal to or greater than $6,000" and no election. (3): an election under s 68AAC(2) counts.
-- (4): exclusions (a)-(d) and "(e) a member to whom the dangerous occupation exception applies".
-- s 68AAC(1): the same bar if "(a) the member is under the age of 25 years" and no election. (3): an election under s 68AAB(2) counts.
-- (4): exclusions (a)-(e).
-- s 68AAD: ss 68AAA-68AAC "do not apply in relation to regulated superannuation funds with no more than 6 members".
--
-- The dangerous occupation exception (s 68AAF) appears in the exclusions of ss 68AAB and 68AAC but NOT of s 68AAA: an emergency
-- services worker whose account goes inactive for 16 months loses default cover like anyone else.
DECLARE Member HAS
    `the fund has no more than 6 members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a defined benefit member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer-sponsor contribution exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dangerous occupation exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `months the account has been inactive` IS A NUMBER
    `account balance` IS A NUMBER
    `has had a balance of $6,000 or more since 1 November 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
    `elected cover despite inactivity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `elected cover despite a low balance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `elected cover while under 25` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a MySuper member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `elected not to have death and incapacity cover` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` IF
        `the member`'s `the fund has no more than 6 members`
    OR  `the member`'s `is a defined benefit member`
    OR  `the member`'s `is a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member`
    OR  `the member`'s `the employer-sponsor contribution exception applies`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68AAA bars cover for an inactive account` IF
        (NOT `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` `the member`)
    AND `the member`'s `months the account has been inactive` AT LEAST 16
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `elected cover despite inactivity`)

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68AAB bars cover for a low balance` IF
        (NOT `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` `the member`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `the dangerous occupation exception applies`)
    AND `the member`'s `account balance` LESS THAN 6000
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `has had a balance of $6,000 or more since 1 November 2019`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `elected cover despite a low balance`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `elected cover while under 25`)

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 68AAC bars cover for a member under 25` IF
        (NOT `outside ss 68AAA-68AAC altogether` `the member`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `the dangerous occupation exception applies`)
    AND `the member`'s `age in years` LESS THAN 25
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `elected cover while under 25`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `elected cover despite a low balance`)

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund may provide insurance cover` IF
        (NOT `s 68AAA bars cover for an inactive account` `the member`)
    AND (NOT `s 68AAB bars cover for a low balance` `the member`)
    AND (NOT `s 68AAC bars cover for a member under 25` `the member`)

-- s 68AA(1): each trustee must ensure "(a) that the fund provides permanent incapacity benefit to each MySuper member"; "(b) ... death
-- benefit"; "(c) ... by taking out insurance". (5): each MySuper member may elect that either or both "will not be provided". (8A),
-- (8B): the section does not require either benefit where s 68AAA, 68AAB or 68AAC stops it being provided by insurance. (9): not for a
-- defined benefit member or a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member. (2), (3): reasonable conditions the trustee
-- determines (for example, the policy's terms) must still be met; they are outside this encoding.
-- (10): "permanent incapacity benefit means a benefit provided ... if, and only if, the member is suffering permanent incapacity";
-- s 10: a member is suffering permanent incapacity "if the member is taken, under the regulations, to be suffering permanent
-- incapacity" -- an INPUT, so the encoding has no rule for it.
GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund must provide default death and incapacity cover` IF
        `the member`'s `is a MySuper member`
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `is a defined benefit member`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `is a permanent or continuous full-time ADF Super member`)
    AND (NOT `the member`'s `elected not to have death and incapacity cover`)
    AND `the fund may provide insurance cover` `the member`

